ently acquired by Golden Cariboo, adjoin the KC claims o","platform":"airborne","year":2008},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":59,"text":"54 g/t Ag 5.73 approximate claim boundary 0.793 g/t Au 0.201 g/t Au .8 Resistivity high linears Anomalous drainage basin Modified by JPEx, August 18, 2026 Figure 20: Rock, Soil and Stream Sediment Geochemistry","year":2026},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":61,"text":"strong historical gold-silver-arsenic soil and a deep, highly conductive VTEM anomaly from BGM\u2019s 2016 survey, which covered the Hixon Gold Block, resulted in the discovery of angular mineralized volcanic boulders in a creek, 58","platform":"airborne","year":2025},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":107,"text":"In 2016, BGM conducted a more than 1350 line kilometre airborne VTEM and magnetic geophysical survey across and adjacent to the Cayenne Project.","platform":"airborne","year":1997,"line_km":350.0},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":108,"text":"were delineated (West and East) based on anomalous copper in soils and IP chargeability highs over the magnetic high anomaly which occurs at the southern contact of the Ste. Marie pluton.","year":2007},{"method":"magnetics","page":108,"text":"Serengeti Resources and Fjordland Exploration completed a detailed airborne magnetic survey followed up by limited soil sampling, prospecting and reconnaissance IP from 2007 to 2014.","platform":"airborne","year":1961},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":114,"text":"Detailed mapping, sampling and evaluation, including soil surveys are recommended to evaluate the following showings and targets within th"},{"method":"magnetics","page":119,"text":"Layman, Maggie, 2017b. Report on the helicopter borne aeromagnetic geophysical survey on the Cayenne property.","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":120,"text":"for Golden Cariboo Resources Ltd. 2018. Geophysical report on IP and resistivity surveys on the Hixon Gold property, Creek, Hixon area, Cariboo Mining Divisio